        <body>
            <div xml:id="d453">

                <pb facs="0668" n="580" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg580"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Newberry to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic">July 21, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received August 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 499.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Replying to your No. 351, of July l,
                    requesting a translation of the “school law” as it now stands, so far as it
                    relates to the interests of citizens of the United States, I have the honor to
                    inclose herewith the information asked for.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. R. Newberry</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d453-a1.xml" xpointer="d453-a1"/>
